WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.000
Not even Scarlett Johansson in a skin-tight
bodysuit could stop the bad reviews haunting

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.130
the 2017 live-action remake of Ghost in the
Shell.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.510
While the film should should serve as a reminder
that adapting anime for the silver screen

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:15.650
isn't as straightforward as one would think,
studios are still determined to keep trying.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.990
A number of U.S. studios have anime adaptations
in production right now, so strap on your

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.279
cat ears, pop open some Pocky, and check out
these anime properties that have upcoming

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.170
live-action remakes.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.480
Death Note

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.439
Based on the manga series of the same name,
the original animated adaptation of Death

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:34.450
Note won an award for Best TV Anime in 2007.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.870
A decade later, there are high hopes for the
American remake.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.530
Adam Wingard, director of the horror-thriller
The Guest, has said that he's enjoyed the

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:46.079
freedom that comes with releasing his live-action
version of Death Note through Netflix, suggesting

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:49.839
that their lack of a rating system means he's
been able to incorporate all the madness of

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:50.839
the original.

00:00:50.839 --> 00:00:55.420
The film, which is due to debut in August
2017, stars Nat Wolff as Light Turner, with

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.260
Willem Dafoe providing the voice of his demon
companion Ryuk.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.160
Which, honestly, isn't too far off.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.360
​Alita: Battle Angel

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:09.840
Produced by James Cameron, Alita: Battle Angel
is an adaptation of a '90s cyberpunk classic.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.400
The Terminator director was first introduced
to the manga series by Hellboy and Pacific

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.470
Rim director Guillermo del Toro — who, knowing
Cameron's body of work, thought he'd be interested

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:19.470
in it.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.500
Laeta Kalogridis was brought on board to pen
the script, and her personal knowledge of

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.130
the property helped bring the remake to life.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:30.090
Directed by Robert Rodriguez and on course
for a July 2018 release, Alita: Battle Angel

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:35.490
stars Maze Runner's Rosa Salazar as Alita,
a cyborg who's been recovered from a scrap

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.880
heap by a cybernetics professor played by
Christoph Waltz.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.000
Michelle Rodriguez and Jennifer Connelly round
out the supporting cast.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.140
​Akira

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:48.920
The Hollywood adaptation of Katsuhiro Otomo's
Akira has been in development hell for so

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.410
long that it's almost become a thing of legend.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:55.180
But recent stirrings about the hunt for a
new director have raised eyebrows again.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:59.810
News of a remake first broke in 2002, but
a mixture of script, casting and budget issues

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:04.860
set it back over the next decade, and it seemed
to have finally been called off in 2012, with

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.870
Warner Bros axing it as part of studio cutbacks.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:11.670
Rumors that the studio was finally ready to
take things forward with Akira began popping

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:16.880
up again in 2016 when Justin Lin was set to
direct, though more recent rumors place Jordan

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.160
Peele at the top of WB's wishlist.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.550
So, has Akira been rescued from development
hell?

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.550
TIme will tell.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.930
Tiger and Bunny

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:29.650
Originally a one-shot published in 2011, Tiger
and Bunny went on to be serialized as a manga

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:33.980
and then adapted into an anime series — all
within the space of a year.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:38.361
Producer/director Ron Howard was first attached
to a live-action version in late 2015, when

00:02:38.361 --> 00:02:43.640
it was announced that his Imagine Entertainment
would join forces with Bandai Namco Pictures.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:48.680
The story takes place in Stern Bild City,
where people known as NEXTs have started developing

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.800
superpowers.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.530
Given Hollywood's obsession with superhero
properties, Tiger and Bunny could potentially

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.810
do big things, but Howard and Namco know that's
a delicate job.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:02.270
Screenwriter Ellen Shanman was given the task,
who Howard called the "perfect match to adapt

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.640
this wildly popular story for new audiences."

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.180
​Fullmetal Alchemist

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.880
Unlike many upcoming anime adaptations, Warner
Bros.' Fullmetal Alchemist live-action remake

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:17.540
is being shot with a Japanese cast, using
Japanese language — which is a little unusual,

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.840
considering the story's set in the fictional
country of Amestris, which is loosely based

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.910
on 19th century Europe.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.720
Director Fumihiko Sori explained,

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:30.380
"I want to create a style that follows the
original manga as much as possible.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.540
The cast is entirely Japanese, but the cultural
background is Europe.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.250
However, it's a style that doesn't represent
a specific race or country.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.990
There will never be a scene in which a character
says something that would identify him/her

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.599
as Japanese."

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:48.710
Japanese fans are reportedly fearing the worst
for Fullmetal Alchemist, which was rated the

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:52.349
second-best anime of all time on My Anime
List.

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:56.840
The film is due out in December 2017, and
based on what's been revealed so far, it'll

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.930
closely follow the plot of the original manga.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.230
​Voltron

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:05.420
Despite Netflix beating Hollywood to the punch
in 2016 with their critically acclaimed, animated

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:10.570
reboot series Voltron: Legendary Defender,
a live-action feature-length remake of the

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:12.860
classic '80s show is still being developed.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.560
Voltron was the brainchild of the late Peter
Keefe, who licensed the giant-robot-based

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.509
Japanese shows "Beast King Go-Lion" and "Armored
Fleet Dairugger XV."

00:04:22.509 --> 00:04:26.809
Keefe's team spliced them together into a
brand new show with overdubbed English dialogue,

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:28.999
creating new stories in the process.

00:04:28.999 --> 00:04:33.689
DreamWorks acquired the rights to a live-action
Voltron film years ago, but when Universal

00:04:33.689 --> 00:04:38.550
bought out the studio toward the end of 2016,
the project ended up in temporary limbo.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.370
More recently, Universal announced that they
still intended to make Voltron, with David

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:46.180
Hayter of X-Men and Watchmen fame on board
to pen the screenplay.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.689
Still no word on who'll form the head, though.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:50.689
​Robotech

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:55.650
Another US anime made from existing Japanese
shows, Robotech combines Macross, Southern

00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:00.620
Cross and Mospeada into a brand new universe
for American audiences.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.949
Director James Wan is a fan, and his knowledge
of the series' origins should serve him well

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:06.850
in the adaptation's creation.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:11.050
The film suffered a setback when rights holders
Harmony Gold disagreed with how Warner Bros.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:14.570
were handling the property and decided to
shack up with Sony instead.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:19.139
There are no official production dates or
cast to announce yet, but we do know Sony

00:05:19.139 --> 00:05:21.599
ordered a page one rewrite of the script.

00:05:21.599 --> 00:05:24.259
So, how close will this skew to the original?

00:05:24.259 --> 00:05:28.590
Harmony Gold's Animation president Tommy Yune
said that we should expect something new,

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.590
saying,

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:30.660
"It's a clean slate.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.990
It may share commonality in that it is based
on the original series, however, the writers

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:37.499
are taking a different approach to it."

00:05:37.499 --> 00:05:39.029
Attack on Titan

00:05:39.029 --> 00:05:44.770
The beautifully brutal manga Attack on Titan
had a whopping 66 million copies in circulation

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:50.719
as of April 2017, and that will only rise
if Warner Bros. can bring their planned live-action

00:05:50.719 --> 00:05:53.430
English language adaptation to the big screen.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:58.080
The story takes place in a world where humanity
lives in a huge walled-off city, which is

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.469
their last defense against the Titans, grotesque,
man-eating giants.

00:06:02.469 --> 00:06:07.189
Attack on Titan has already been adapted into
a two-part movie in Japan, and not completely

00:06:07.189 --> 00:06:08.349
successfully.

00:06:08.349 --> 00:06:12.900
Despite the earlier adaptation's setbacks,
Warner Bros. intends to remake these two films

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.219
rather than adapt their own version directly
from the original manga.

00:06:16.219 --> 00:06:20.949
Deadline reports that Warner Bros is locked
in negotiations over the remake rights, with

00:06:20.949 --> 00:06:24.979
Harry Potter producer David Heyman lined up
to take charge of the project.

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:29.809
If the studio fails to strike a deal, others
will soon be lining up to make their own pitch

00:06:29.809 --> 00:06:34.660
and a Hollywood remake of Attack on Titan
seems like merely a matter of time.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.660
Naruto

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:41.439
In 2016, respected manga magazine Shonen Jump
revealed that a Hollywood remake of Naruto

00:06:41.439 --> 00:06:46.259
was in the works under the guidance of Lionsgate
Studios and director Michael Gracey.

00:06:46.259 --> 00:06:51.569
In terms of source material, the original
Naruto series consisted of 220 episodes, and

00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:56.999
Naruto: Shippuden aired a whopping 500 installments,
so the filmmakers certainly won't run short

00:06:56.999 --> 00:06:59.689
on ideas should this film develop into a franchise.

00:06:59.689 --> 00:07:05.119
And considering who's producing, Marvel Studios
co-founder and former chief executive Avi

00:07:05.119 --> 00:07:07.580
Arad, that's a very real possibility.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:11.360
If anyone knows how to transition from print
to the screen, it's him.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:15.309
Wary of superhero fatigue among audiences,
he went looking for a new angle.

00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:19.279
According to his son and partner Ari, they're
working on creating an "incredibly visual

00:07:19.279 --> 00:07:20.379
and cool world."

00:07:20.379 --> 00:07:24.110
Hopefully the two will have learned some valuable
lessons after what happened with that other

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:28.369
big anime movie they produced, 2017's Ghost
in the Shell...

00:07:28.369 --> 00:07:29.839
Thanks for watching!

00:07:29.839 --> 00:07:32.130
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.939
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

